{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":1,"delta":"{\"path\":\"/workspace/out/root_cause.json\",\"content\":\"{\\n  \\\"incident_id\\\": \\\"072-064-service-dependency-triage\\\",\\n  \\\"root_cause_service\\\": \\\"auth-gateway\\\",\\n  \\\"root_cause_change_id\\\": \\\"AUTH-2026-0318\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n  \\\"affected_services\\\": [\\n    \\\"checkout-web\\\",\\n    \\\"payment-api\\\",\\n    \\\"auth-gateway\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"source_file\\\": \\\"/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log\\\",\\n      \\\"observation\\\": \\\"At 2026-03-22T14:05:12Z auth-gateway deployed change AUTH-2026-0318, setting jwks_namespace=partner-v2 and issuer=partner-v2.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source_file\\\": \\\"/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log\\\",\\n      \\\"observation\\\": \\\"At 2026-03-22T14:08:34Z auth-gateway logged validation failed reason=issuer_not_allowed with token_issuer=partner-v2 while allowed_issuers remained partner-v1, which shows a bad issuer configuration after the change.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source_file\\\": \\\"/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log\\\",\\n      \\\"observation\\\": \\\"payment-api rejected checkout request req-8812 because auth-gateway returned issuer_not_allowed / invalid_issuer before any order-db work.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source_file\\\": \\\"/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log\\\",\\n      \\\"observation\\\": \\\"checkout-web failed submit_order with status=401 from payment-api and logged auth_failed invalid issuer, matching the downstream auth break.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source_file\\\": \\\"/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv\\\",\\n      \\\"observation\\\": \\\"At 14:10Z, auth-gateway 401 rate rose to 28.4, payment-api 401 rate rose to 21.2, and checkout-web 401 rate rose to 18.7, showing the failure propagated along the checkout dependency chain.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source_file\\\": \\\"/workspace/in/topology.json\\\",\\n      \\\"observation\\\": \\\"Topology shows checkout-web depends on payment-api, which depends on auth-gateway; AUTH-2026-0318 is the only recent auth-gateway change listed.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"excluded_red_herrings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"signal\\\": \\\"orders-db CPU spike / DB-2026-0144\\\",\\n      \\\"why_not_primary\\\": \\\"orders-db metrics show p95 query latency normal and errors=0, payment-api states order-db was not used before the auth gate on failing requests, and orders-db logged that failed checkout request req-8812 never reached it.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"signal\\\": \\\"cdn-edge 5xx / CDN-2026-0091\\\",\\n      \\\"why_not_primary\\\": \\\"cdn-edge errors were isolated to static images, checkout-web logged static assets served normally after retry, and user checkout remained blocked by payment auth failures rather than asset delivery.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"recommended_next_steps\\\": [\\n    \\\"Mitigate now by restoring allowed_issuers to include partner-v2 or by rolling back AUTH-2026-0318 on auth-gateway.\\\",\\n    \\\"Flush or rebuild the JWKS cache namespace so partner-v2 tokens resolve without fallback to partner-v1 settings.\\\",\\n    \\\"Verify after mitigation that auth-gateway no longer logs issuer_not_allowed for partner-v2 tokens and that payment-api invalid_issuer errors stop.\\\",\\n    \\\"Confirm checkout-web submit_order requests return to normal success/latency and 401 rates drop across auth-gateway, payment-api, and checkout-web.\\\",\\n    \\\"Add a config validation or canary check to catch issuer/JWKS namespace mismatches before deploy.\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\"}"}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_aYL76qbUNQ6a0Pho6PnepjMW|fc_0fa14be1de3d34fb016a95ad61e98087d282e75b4ff0804166","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/out/root_cause.json","content":"{\n  \"incident_id\": \"072-064-service-dependency-triage\",\n  \"root_cause_service\": \"auth-gateway\",\n  \"root_cause_change_id\": \"AUTH-2026-0318\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"affected_services\": [\n    \"checkout-web\",\n    \"payment-api\",\n    \"auth-gateway\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log\",\n      \"observation\": \"At 2026-03-22T14:05:12Z auth-gateway deployed change AUTH-2026-0318, setting jwks_namespace=partner-v2 and issuer=partner-v2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log\",\n      \"observation\": \"At 2026-03-22T14:08:34Z auth-gateway logged validation failed reason=issuer_not_allowed with token_issuer=partner-v2 while allowed_issuers remained partner-v1, which shows a bad issuer configuration after the change.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log\",\n      \"observation\": \"payment-api rejected checkout request req-8812 because auth-gateway returned issuer_not_allowed / invalid_issuer before any order-db work.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log\",\n      \"observation\": \"checkout-web failed submit_order with status=401 from payment-api and logged auth_failed invalid issuer, matching the downstream auth break.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv\",\n      \"observation\": \"At 14:10Z, auth-gateway 401 rate rose to 28.4, payment-api 401 rate rose to 21.2, and checkout-web 401 rate rose to 18.7, showing the failure propagated along the checkout dependency chain.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/topology.json\",\n      \"observation\": \"Topology shows checkout-web depends on payment-api, which depends on auth-gateway; AUTH-2026-0318 is the only recent auth-gateway change listed.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"excluded_red_herrings\": [\n    {\n      \"signal\": \"orders-db CPU spike / DB-2026-0144\",\n      \"why_not_primary\": \"orders-db metrics show p95 query latency normal and errors=0, payment-api states order-db was not used before the auth gate on failing requests, and orders-db logged that failed checkout request req-8812 never reached it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"signal\": \"cdn-edge 5xx / CDN-2026-0091\",\n      \"why_not_primary\": \"cdn-edge errors were isolated to static images, checkout-web logged static assets served normally after retry, and user checkout remained blocked by payment auth failures rather than asset delivery.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recommended_next_steps\": [\n    \"Mitigate now by restoring allowed_issuers to include partner-v2 or by rolling back AUTH-2026-0318 on auth-gateway.\",\n    \"Flush or rebuild the JWKS cache namespace so partner-v2 tokens resolve without fallback to partner-v1 settings.\",\n    \"Verify after mitigation that auth-gateway no longer logs issuer_not_allowed for partner-v2 tokens and that payment-api invalid_issuer errors stop.\",\n    \"Confirm checkout-web submit_order requests return to normal success/latency and 401 rates drop across auth-gateway, payment-api, and checkout-web.\",\n    \"Add a config validation or canary check to catch issuer/JWKS namespace mismatches before deploy.\"\n  ]\n}"}}}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_start","contentIndex":2}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":2,"delta":"{\"path\":\"/workspace/out/triage_notes.md\",\"content\":\"# Checkout incident triage notes\\n\\n## Dependency path\\nDirectly observed path from user impact to root cause:\\n\\n1. `checkout-web` returned checkout submit failures with `401` from `payment-api` (`/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log`).\\n2. `payment-api` rejected the same flow because token validation failed at `auth-gateway` with `invalid_issuer` / `issuer_not_allowed` (`/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log`).\\n3. `auth-gateway` had just deployed `AUTH-2026-0318`, then logged a `partner-v2` token issuer against `allowed_issuers=partner-v1`, which is the first clear broken condition in the chain (`/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log`).\\n4. `topology.json` matches this path: `checkout-web -> payment-api -> auth-gateway` (`/workspace/in/topology.json`).\\n\\n## Directly observed facts\\n- `/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log` shows `AUTH-2026-0318` deployed at `2026-03-22T14:05:12Z` with `jwks_namespace=partner-v2 issuer=partner-v2`.\\n- The same log shows `validation failed reason=issuer_not_allowed token_issuer=partner-v2 allowed_issuers=partner-v1` at `2026-03-22T14:08:34Z`.\\n- `/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log` shows `create_payment` rejected `req-8812` with `auth_result=invalid_issuer` and says `order-db dependency not used before auth gate for failing requests`.\\n- `/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log` shows checkout submit failed with `status=401 upstream=payment-api` and `invalid issuer`.\\n- `/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv` shows a sharp 401 rise at 14:10Z in `auth-gateway` (28.4), `payment-api` (21.2), and `checkout-web` (18.7).\\n- `/workspace/in/logs/orders-db.log` shows `errors=0`, `p95_query_ms=35`, and that failed request `req-8812` never reached `orders-db`.\\n\\n## Inferences\\n- High-confidence root cause: `auth-gateway` change `AUTH-2026-0318` left issuer validation out of sync with the new `partner-v2` issuer/JWKS namespace.\\n- The user-visible checkout failure is a dependency cascade, not an app-only bug in `checkout-web`.\\n- `orders-db` and `cdn-edge` produced noise during the incident window but did not drive the blocked checkout path.\\n\\n## Red herrings excluded\\n- **orders-db CPU spike**: directly observed CPU was high, but latency stayed normal and no failing checkout reached the DB. So this is not the primary cause.\\n- **cdn-edge 5xx on images**: directly observed as isolated to static assets; checkout-web logged assets recovered while checkout stayed blocked by auth.\\n\\n## Immediate mitigation\\n1. Roll back `AUTH-2026-0318` on `auth-gateway`, or restore `allowed_issuers` so `partner-v2` is accepted.\\n2. Clear or rebuild the JWKS cache namespace so lookups do not fall back from `partner-v2` to `partner-v1`.\\n3. Watch `auth-gateway`, `payment-api`, and `checkout-web` for 401 drop after the fix.\\n\\n## Verification steps\\n1. Replay or inspect a fresh checkout and confirm `checkout-web` no longer logs `submit_order failed status=401 upstream=payment-api`.\\n2. Confirm `payment-api` stops logging `auth_result=invalid_issuer`.\\n3. Confirm `auth-gateway` stops logging `issuer_not_allowed` for `token_issuer=partner-v2`.\\n4. Check service metrics for 401 rates and latency returning toward the 14:00Z baseline in `/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv`.\\n5. Confirm no new blocker appears downstream once auth passes, including a quick check that `orders-db` remains error-free.\\n\"}"}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_uWTRl0ApbSdOv5UnohiacW1C|fc_0fa14be1de3d34fb016a95ad61e99887d280f134f3fc21834c","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/out/triage_notes.md","content":"# Checkout incident triage notes\n\n## Dependency path\nDirectly observed path from user impact to root cause:\n\n1. `checkout-web` returned checkout submit failures with `401` from `payment-api` (`/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log`).\n2. `payment-api` rejected the same flow because token validation failed at `auth-gateway` with `invalid_issuer` / `issuer_not_allowed` (`/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log`).\n3. `auth-gateway` had just deployed `AUTH-2026-0318`, then logged a `partner-v2` token issuer against `allowed_issuers=partner-v1`, which is the first clear broken condition in the chain (`/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log`).\n4. `topology.json` matches this path: `checkout-web -> payment-api -> auth-gateway` (`/workspace/in/topology.json`).\n\n## Directly observed facts\n- `/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log` shows `AUTH-2026-0318` deployed at `2026-03-22T14:05:12Z` with `jwks_namespace=partner-v2 issuer=partner-v2`.\n- The same log shows `validation failed reason=issuer_not_allowed token_issuer=partner-v2 allowed_issuers=partner-v1` at `2026-03-22T14:08:34Z`.\n- `/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log` shows `create_payment` rejected `req-8812` with `auth_result=invalid_issuer` and says `order-db dependency not used before auth gate for failing requests`.\n- `/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log` shows checkout submit failed with `status=401 upstream=payment-api` and `invalid issuer`.\n- `/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv` shows a sharp 401 rise at 14:10Z in `auth-gateway` (28.4), `payment-api` (21.2), and `checkout-web` (18.7).\n- `/workspace/in/logs/orders-db.log` shows `errors=0`, `p95_query_ms=35`, and that failed request `req-8812` never reached `orders-db`.\n\n## Inferences\n- High-confidence root cause: `auth-gateway` change `AUTH-2026-0318` left issuer validation out of sync with the new `partner-v2` issuer/JWKS namespace.\n- The user-visible checkout failure is a dependency cascade, not an app-only bug in `checkout-web`.\n- `orders-db` and `cdn-edge` produced noise during the incident window but did not drive the blocked checkout path.\n\n## Red herrings excluded\n- **orders-db CPU spike**: directly observed CPU was high, but latency stayed normal and no failing checkout reached the DB. So this is not the primary cause.\n- **cdn-edge 5xx on images**: directly observed as isolated to static assets; checkout-web logged assets recovered while checkout stayed blocked by auth.\n\n## Immediate mitigation\n1. Roll back `AUTH-2026-0318` on `auth-gateway`, or restore `allowed_issuers` so `partner-v2` is accepted.\n2. Clear or rebuild the JWKS cache namespace so lookups do not fall back from `partner-v2` to `partner-v1`.\n3. Watch `auth-gateway`, `payment-api`, and `checkout-web` for 401 drop after the fix.\n\n## Verification steps\n1. Replay or inspect a fresh checkout and confirm `checkout-web` no longer logs `submit_order failed status=401 upstream=payment-api`.\n2. Confirm `payment-api` stops logging `auth_result=invalid_issuer`.\n3. Confirm `auth-gateway` stops logging `issuer_not_allowed` for `token_issuer=partner-v2`.\n4. Check service metrics for 401 rates and latency returning toward the 14:00Z baseline in `/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv`.\n5. Confirm no new blocker appears downstream once auth passes, including a quick check that `orders-db` remains error-free.\n"}}}}
